he results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two specimens  Labeled  Right breast  is a 20 x 15 x 3cm mastectomy specimen  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple and areola complex  and a suture designating superior aspect  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm ill defined  tan white  firm area located in the medial aspect of the specimen  and focally extends to 0 3cm from both the anterior and posterior resection margin  Representative sections of the tumor are submitted in cassettes A F  A C  Tumor in relationship to the closest anterior resection margin  D F  Tumor in relationship to the closest posterior resection margin   The remaining breast parenchyma shows fibrocystic changes  Representative sections of the fibrocystic area are submitted in cassettes G I  Labeled  Right axillary content  is a 7 x 5 x 1 5cm fatty adipose tissue  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes J Q  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST  MASTECTOMY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , 1.
